## Semantic spacing (gap, padding, margin)

Use **`$gap-*`**, **`$padding-horizontal-*` / `$padding-vertical-*`**, **`$margin-horizontal-*` / `$margin-vertical-*`** from `_number.scss` instead of raw `px` in new or heavily edited SCSS.

### Gap scale

For **which gap to use where**, see the vertical rhythm quick-reference table in **`design.mdc` §8.1a**.

| Variable | Value | When to use |
|----------|--------|-------------|
| `$gap-xs` | 0px | Flush stacks; SectionHeader → Card (no extra gap) |
| `$gap-s` | 2px | Tight decorative steps |
| `$gap-m` | 4px | Within a text cluster: title → supporting line, label → icon |
| `$gap-l` | 6px | Slightly looser cluster interior |
| `$gap-xl` | 8px | Chip → Chip in a row; comfortable inline gaps; **Header (large) → first section cluster**; tighter end of cluster spacing |
| `$gap-2xl` | 12px | Between separate clusters on the same surface; SectionHeader trailing cluster |
| `$gap-3xl` | 16px | Inside Card body stacks (TextField → TextField, Search → Tabs, Tabs → body); between clusters in sheets |
| `$gap-4xl` | 24px | **Between sections** on the page (separate Card **groups** / section blocks). **Not** for dense **stacked** plan/tile **Card** lists — use **`$margin-horizontal-m` (12px)** vertical gap there so rhythm matches the page gutter (**`design.mdc` §8.1a**). |
| `$gap-5xl` | 32px | Optional larger break between sections when a product spec asks (not the default after **Header** **large**) |

### Padding / margin semantics (selected)

| Variable | Value | Notes |
|----------|--------|--------|
| `$padding-horizontal-3xl` / `$padding-vertical-3xl` | 16px | Common **component horizontal inset** (e.g. `SectionHeader`, list rows, OTP container) |
| `$padding-horizontal-2xl` / `$padding-vertical-2xl` | 12px | Medium horizontal / vertical steps |
| `$margin-horizontal-m` | 12px | Common **page gutter** in framed mobile previews (**`.cursor/design.mdc` §9**) |

**Root Vite app** (`src/index.css`): keeps **typography** CSS variables for global header tweaks only—compose spacing with **library SCSS tokens** (`$gap-*`, `$padding-*`) or **`var(--…)`** from `variables.css`.

