## Typography (`_typography.scss` + mixins)

**Font stack:** `inter-subset` with system UI fallbacks — defined in `sass-generated/index.css`.

**Weights:** `$typography-weight-regular` (400), `$typography-weight-medium` (500), `$typography-weight-semibold` (600), `$typography-weight-bold` (700).

### Type scale (size / line-height)

| Step | Font size | Line height |
|------|-----------|---------------|
| display1 | 42px | 48px |
| display2 | 36px | 40px |
| display3 | 32px | 36px |
| title1 | 22px | 28px |
| title2 | 20px | 24px |
| title3 | 18px | 24px |
| title4 | 16px | 20px |
| body | 14px | 20px |
| subtext | 12px | 16px |
| caption | 10px | 12px |

**In code:** use **`@include getFontStyle(<scale>-<weight>, <color>);`** (see `paytm-common-storybook/src/commonStyles/_mixin.scss` and existing `*.module.scss` files).

### Section titles (`SectionHeader`)

Use the **`SectionHeader`** component; do not recreate the same hierarchy with ad-hoc classes.

**Default `size`:** **`extra-large`** (component default in `SectionHeader.tsx` — **`title1-bold`**). Pass **`medium`**, **`large`**, or **`small`** only when the screen needs a smaller section title.

Rough mapping (`SectionHeader.module.scss`):

| `size` prop | Title style |
|-------------|-------------|
| `small` | `body-bold` |
| `medium` | `title3-bold` |
| `large` | `title2-bold` |
| `extra-large` | `title1-bold` |

Padding on the container: **`$padding-vertical-xl $padding-horizontal-3xl`** (8px vertical, 16px horizontal).

### Large `HeaderDefault` second-row title

Per **`.cursor/design.mdc` §3.4:** the primary screen title on **`HeaderDefault`** `size="large"` uses **display3 + bold** and **`var(--text-neutral-strong)`** — do not duplicate that headline with a `SectionHeader` for the same string.

