## Semantic colours (`variables.css`)

Use **`var(--…)`** names from `variables.css` in UI (not hard-coded hex), except in token source files.

**Theme:** default light in `:root`; **dark** swaps values under **`@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)`** (same variable names).

### Surfaces (example)

| Token | Role |
|--------|------|
| `--surface-level-1` … `--surface-level-4` | Page / layer surfaces |
| `--background-neutral-*` | Strong / medium / weak / inverse fills |

### Text (common)

| Token | Role |
|--------|------|
| `--text-neutral-strong` | Primary headings / strongest body |
| `--text-neutral-moderate` | Secondary body |
| `--text-neutral-medium` | Tertiary / de-emphasis |
| `--text-primary-strong` / `--text-primary-medium` | Brand / links |
| `--text-positive-strong` / `--text-negative-strong` / `--text-notice-strong` | Status |

### Borders (common)

| Token | Role |
|--------|------|
| `--border-neutral-weak` | Hairlines, dividers |
| `--border-neutral-strong` / `--border-primary-medium` | Stronger strokes when needed |

**Full set:** `variables.css` (light block + dark media query). **Role tables:** `.cursor/design.mdc` §2.

