## Component spacing notes (reference implementations)

Values below reflect current **`*.module.scss`**; when extending, match these patterns.

### Button (`Button.module.scss`)

| Topic | Value / pattern |
|--------|------------------|
| Label ↔ icon | `$gap-m` (4px) in `.titleSection` |
| Heights | Large **52px**, medium **32px**, small **24px** (fixed, not gap tokens) |
| Medium horizontal padding | `$padding-vertical-xs $padding-horizontal-2xl` |

### Section header (`SectionHeader.module.scss`)

| Topic | Value / pattern |
|--------|------------------|
| Container padding | `$padding-vertical-xl $padding-horizontal-3xl` |
| First row gap (title ↔ trailing) | `$gap-3xl` (16px) |
| Trailing cluster | `$gap-2xl` (12px) |

### Lists (`List.module.scss` patterns)

List rows use **`$padding-horizontal-3xl`** for horizontal inset; hairline/offset math is component-specific — see `.cursor/design.mdc` for full-bleed and card-composition rules.

---

## Layout conventions (token-backed)

| Topic | Rule |
|--------|------|
| Page gutter (framed preview / app shell) | **`$margin-horizontal-m`** (**12px**) — see **`.cursor/design.mdc` §9**; adjust only with design agreement |
| Semantic colours | Always **`var(--text-*)`**, **`var(--surface-*)`**, **`var(--border-*)`**, etc., from `variables.css` |
| Library spacing | Prefer **`$gap-*` / `$padding-*` / `$unit-*`** over literals in `paytm-common-storybook` SCSS |
| Cards + lists | Card owns content inset; avoid **double horizontal inset** when nesting `ListItem` — see **`.cursor/design.mdc` §9 / §11** (strip duplicate row padding in the owning surface when needed) |
| Dark mode | Rely on **`prefers-color-scheme`** in `variables.css`; do not hand-pick separate dark hex in app code |

